      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1897-12-31_WidnesExaminer_art0031" n="art0031">
        <head>OIL WELLS OF CALIFORNIA.</head>
        <p>THE OIL WELLS OF CALIFORNIA.</p>
        <p>-- The exidence of pot oleurnspring. wan known to the early neaten in California, and it is reported that asphaltum was found by the aborigines along the coast, being walked in by the net, and used by them hoover,- 00n pineal's. Oil wells were sunk at Santa Paula, Loa Angeles County, some time after the eettlement. and later an oil-producing belt was diecovered at Puente, and again at Summerland, below Santa Barbara, where • singular state of affair. prints. It teems soon op potent at the latter locolity that the Oil bearing stratum stretched far out into the out, and drill scaffoldings he- pa in a short time to extend from inland and to creep up the shore in the direction of Santa Barbara. At first they kept along the side. of the hills browning the sea there, but gradually they turned inward until one at length rod from the water. Work wan darted at an extremely one tide, and finally the scaffeldine appeared 201 t. or 301 t. from the shore. At present there are three borings, which, tenant low tide, are in the neater, but at Rood-tide are completely eurrounded, the men working on platforms of various heights, which they midwife', ascend as the sea rises. Se for the structures that have been erect oti in the da have not experienced a strong eouth-weeter,but as some of them Add in eft. of water or more at high tide,in • severe storm their existence will become precarious. The drids are worked in the water from an engine on the beach,the fuel being the oil pumped up. This is probably the only place where the oil is pumped out of the sea ; hut undoubtedly the entire coast overlie. an olleproducing stratum. Off what is known as Afore's Wharf, half • mile out,oil ride to the surface in eeveral plum. Probably one of the etrangeet eights of oil wells siren In Los Angel... In Chet city oil was liret dis- covered in its western portion, but daffoldings began to rise no rapidly that in a short titre the place seemed to bristle with them. The beet reeideneee were ruined by the proximity of the unsightly objects, and finally the whole place wee given Over to the oil drilLand at present it resembles certain portions of the oil region of Pennsylvania. The boring. bad advanced in a well- defined north.easevly direction, and at pedant oppear , to be stopped he the cemetery, which Overlie. the oil • stratum. Not far distance ia the Lon Angeles river, which probably will ultimately be encroached on. The discovery of oil In and about Lou Angeles promises soon to supply the long wished for power required for mead . factoring purpled The Terminal Railroad boa adopted the oil as fuel, and the Southern Pacific is said to he ex- perimenting in alike direction. As Chiltern'a fit with- • out coal depoeits, if we exoept lignito bode, which crop tett in various places, oil as • fuel will supply a want long felt at Log Angeles, and become • factor le the rapid development of the city.</p>
