        <p>tile waves on accompaniment. Iby carnally replacing too tern .. vegeta no reply, and I dui not speak again, but lay the raii.e 01 death became known Stanhope. who was in Hatening totbe ma and thinking of my own affairs, gaol awaiting trial for forgery, sem charged with the murder, but he had nothing to say. He had told the All at once ha jumped up, and after taking several pnlicpe,wodli.e,n,:r.resr.etede.pthat Hawthorae bad cleared out, rapid strides tip and down, he sat down on a bit M t for the tools, which he said be rock close by no. • IC. no use, Hugh,' he burst nn u ! had bought. Sobesquently he confessed the receipt was out at last, ' I !an endure it no longer, I must leave a forgery,but alleged the. he had received romipt,but home again.' • Leave home?' 1 echoed. fairly! lost it, and forged another. Stanhope is also said to bewHdered by I hi. sudden avowal. ' What do you have confeesed that he had committed bigamy. The wean? It It best to tell you all, he mad.' Oh. ! police have a letter purporting to have been written by Hugh! I cannot help loving (iwendolimi, It,, net M is. Stanhope at Ilawthorne's dictation to Hawthorne's icy fault, I have striven against it, but staying sister. Mating that Hawthorne had poi/Med hi. right near her only makes it harder to bear. Yon hams hand, and had not been able to work for three week.. the prior right, and lam in honour bound to leave antiAlOp wan made in it to Stanhrgm's kindness to him, the place. He tried to speak calmly and .nd there was a postscript, signed H.M 5.," deprecate mg Hawthorne'. allusion to his kindness. Hawthorne indifferently, lad the emotion which refused to list tanned by a alight qnrrae in ha, had disappeared • week or ten day. before the date of this letter. another letter, with a still later date, was voice. !addressed tb the murdered man, and stated that he (Hawthorne) had taken away £B7 from Stanhope'. bog, HAVE YOU PAIN P which Hawthorne had given tom to mind, and for which Hawthorn