        <p>OUR LOCAL CHURCHES. CHRISTMAS CASITALTII WARRINGTON. About two o'clock en Friday afternoon named Frank Monks and • companion ni Hughes, were out ferreting and emoting r. an the occupation of Mr. Haddock, near to bloat Railway...hen a rabbit bolted and Hughes shot at It with • gun he arm carrying. Unfortunately he missed hie aim, and the whole of the charge entered Moth's left thigh at the bock, creating terrible injurlos. IMortniation taunt ones given to P.C.'s Johnson sod lifeath,who were on duty in Btooks-lane.and with all pos- sible haste they went to the injured man and stopped the bleeding and temporarily hound op the injury,which eras of • serious and extensive nature. This having been done the pollee ambulance was procured, and Monk. wan carried on this to where:a lorry was in wait- egos which he was immediately conveyed to the War- rington Infirmary. where he wan attended to by the home surgeons. The promptitude of the police in stopping the bleeding undoubtedly prevented Monks bleeding to death. Ehe injured lad's leg was amputated en Sunday. An accident occurred in Crosfieldatniet. on Friday, to a boa newid Arthur Roberts (ton), Wan live, in deploy- street, Be was endeavouring to crone Crosfield-street when he wan knocked down by • passing cab, sustain- ing • wound on the left leg. Ho was removed to the In- firmary for treatment, and is progressing very satisfac. torily. On Saturday night,* woman named 'Dixon, living in Foundry-street. pouted acme oil on her fre,which caused dames to shoot up and ignite the mantel border. She ran out of the howl. screaming, and attracte I by her Deputy-Superintendent Frank Turner and Fireman . . .</p>
        <p>ST. PAUL'S CHURCH. At the close of the usual rervice at St. Paul's Church, on Sunday evening, one or two Chriatmas carol, were trivert by the choir al well as some special music, Mr. willies, organist, conducting. 'The programme was opened with an excellent rendering of the anthem la the beginning was the word " Tarns Tozer). Mr. J. H. Sherlock, afterwards nog in good style the solo, " Calvary." Mies Brough was heard to advantage ix the rolo He shall feed His flock," and Mr D Poishaw sang with considerable taste and erpremion Nazareth." The carols were especially well sung, and the programme was concluded by • very spirited render- ing of the Hallelujah Chortle. PRIMITIVE MEIHODIST CHAPEL, LISGH-STREET. •Cbristmas eong service was beld in the Primitive Methodist Chapel, Legit... Civet, on Sundoy evening. The denim which wait Well attended wax of an intereating and instructive character. The Rev. C. Finch preached upon "The Wire Men from the Ewa.. The carols, Christians Awake"' Hark the Herald Angels Sing," and other, were sung by the ,:ongregstion. Sir.. Moorm gang Why Jesus tame," and another solo ; Mr. A. Spr!ice " The Sanctuary," and Mr. Coffin" Comfort ye. The choir tendered two anthems. The commerce. Donal singing was hearty, and the win. and anthems were rendered lea matter that reflocted credit upon sublet and choir, Mr. A. Spruce eonducted the singing, and Mr. A. L. Finch preridei at the organ. Mr. Brad- . bury gave ashore report of the working of the church daring the ;AM year, and pointed out that the school</p>
