        <head>GRAPPENHALL.</head>
        <p>GRAPPENHALL.</p>
        <p>nem COUNCIL Man. —This Council met under tbe chairmanship of Mr. J. C. Parr. at the schoolroom, on Tuesday night. Mr. Long reported the result of the inquiry at Hout.ford concerning the proposed alteration of the county boundary. He said the bulk of the local authorities affected were opposed to the alteration unless compensation were given. The comnsittes appointed to attend to the safety of the footway •CrOgn the Ship Canal locks reported that the Ship Canal Company had dose theis utomet in the way of affording protection to the public, but they still urged the necessity of provid- ing lights at night in order to obviate accidents. Mr. Jenkins said nothing had yet been door about Johnson'. charity. It was decided to have a parish meeting to disco...the subject.—Mr. Boardman remarked that • call of £2O for lighting bad been received from the Run- corn Rural District Council, and the accounts did not specify what it was for. A reply was received from Mr. Ashton, the clerk, stating that the account was for two years.</p>
      </div>
