        <p>Christmas bag come and gone, and generally spewing, the Yuletide cot 1897 has been as enjoy. stole as asp of ate pretionessors. So much depends, during those national holidays, on the wcather,that it wne an unalloyed plea.co to all When the min canoed felling, and King Frost assumed away over the element,. The hastiness of the air was sufficient to cover we slmllo a, pools and II coded Meadows with a smooth icy rumen, width was productive of enjoyment to tuousands on Friday and Saturday. Lice principal resorts were the Tiviggenus and Long- ford, Where every facility for participation in the exhilarating winter p.c.., was afforded. There were the usual rejoicings and feastings at the Work- house, Fidgets ludustrial Schools, intirmary and Hospital, the Barracks, and at the Drill HMI, where ' , the poor were regaled. Serene, wer, held at many ' ol toe churches, in the morning. An ele cent of witness was lent to the celebration by the unnual number of c.tialtino during the week end. One, • burning accident to a little girl,' has had a fatal termination, While all have been, serious to the people most I=mo-in:Hely affected.; The great attraction of a mann at Wildempoil be.' tween Warrington and Widnes, drew an immense crowd. Ordinaroy a crush is safely dealt with by the oliciale,bue on this occasion flit said that some I impatient individual opened the big gate, with the I recoil that in the rush several people were craned and one youth was so injured that his detention at the infirmary was necessitated. Tne holiday on Monday was observed by nearly everybody. Train- men closed early er else never operted,and the sari.' o. works also presented an appearance of ' quietude. The streets were full of a holiday crowd, though many persons /*sited Liverpool end Man. Oriole. Where the Christmas pan, ono.. are in lull swing. There wae rather a big qdantity Of tui? druukennessa surprising percentage of the publi p being untnistaknbly. under the potent spell of 1 irim or 