      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1897-12-31_WidnesExaminer_art0069" n="art0069">
        <head>BURNING FATALI;Ii AT WARRINGTON.</head>
        <p>BURNING FATALI;Ii AT WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>Mr. F. A. Jones, deputy coroner, conducted an in. 'Meilen to the death of Jane Lawless, 10 years of age, who died on Moodily at the Infirmary from barns received on Sunday.—Annie Moiseley, 2 Bakehouse- yasd,mother of deceased said on Sunday the latter came in for dinner.about 5 minuted to 3 o'clock. Witness ea, her her dinner and told her to take it to the •• chip " shop and eat it thee, Witnesa's sister, Sarah Lawless hoed at the" chip "shoo. In less than flay minutes a girl tarot, to witness, who went to the shop and found deceased Waeing. Waness could do nothing for her when nose •••• her blaZing, and went into the street, to call for help. Efer husband estinguiehed the fiamee.—Margaret McCone, a child of about eight, said she waa playing with deceased in the +hop. There w... • fire which . deceased had liehted. She was standing on • form in ! front of the Are eating her dinner from the mantelpiece and while to doing her clothes caught flee—Sarah Law- less. whose hinds were bandaged from the effect ef burns. saidebe knevr the children were playing in her shop when she hrael screams and rushed in the room. Deceised was on fire, end witness beat it out with her hands an well en she could. Witnesa wan also badly burnt.—Nune Isherwood said that deceased whoa admit- ted into the Infirmary oo Sunday between 3 30 and 4 p cc. She aria aoffering from burns on the bole of a severe nature. Deceased expired at 5 on Monday. —A verdict of " Accident•l death was returned."</p>
