        <head>WARRINGTON GROUND REPORTED.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON GROUND REPORTED.</p>
        <p>' At a meeting of the committee, in Manchester, on Tuesday night, Mr. Hancock, of Runcorn, the referee In the Warrington and Widnes match tut Saturday, re. ported the Warrington air c atom for unruly condu..t. • and the officials were ordered to post 200 warning notices all over the town. Mr. Hancock likewise reported Naylor, • Warrington forward, for wrongful language, and be was suspended for one month. Mr. Wright, of Runcorn, the referee in the A "teem match between the same clubs, repined Foster, of Widnes, and the matter was adjourned until the neat meeting. rim mewl., between Stoughton Rangers and Stockport and &amp;lord and Richdals Hornets on Christmas Day were ' ordered to be repl iyed ' • and the instal between Tyldes. Icy and Wigan, played as a friendly, was ordered to N,Ofi an a League contest. Widnes were heed 31s. and Tyldealey DD. for late smite. Rochdale Hornets sub- mitred cope of the warning bill they had been ordered to post and same Ira. considered satisfactory. Elrarnhall, of Warrington St. Mary's, was suspended Ass die ;R, Moore, of Miiions, far three weeks and Crorsley. of St. ' Helens, and Hopwood, of Barton, for a fortnight.</p>
