      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1897-12-31_WidnesExaminer_art0087" n="art0087">
        <head>WARRINGTON</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON</p>
        <p>SPIRITUALISM</p>
        <p>Dn. Waddilove,of bawds Hs% Peseta wan the opeaker on Sunday afternoon and evening at the Spirit.lint meetings in the Amideniy-street Teta- wanes Sall, and delivered two good addretteaDhe wan fairly accessfu in her clairvoyance. The at- tendance wee not no good as Mal. SCDIMI DEATH ST WALTON An inquest was held by Mr. Woreley on Tuesday on the body of John 1hr1e,34 VMS of age, who lived at 18, Eatfordeetreet, Waltomend who was found dad in bed on Sunday afternoon. Dr Parker attributed death to at total causes, and a verdict to this effect fins returned. The Inguset was held at the deceased'. hott-e.</p>
