        <p>THE PROPOSED NEW BRIDGE ACROSS THE ItEnSET AT WARRINGTON. bast werk, • committee Of the County Coun- cil, consisting of Alderman F. I. Armitage, £l4el- - C. OvilowJecksonAuil Alderman John Stierley with Mr F. C. Melton (clerk to the County Council) made an inspection of Warringtoo Bridge, in com- p., with the Mayor (Alderman Wright), member, of the Town Council, and officials of the Corpora- tion. The deputation did not •isit the town speci- ally for t his row., but is order to hold an in- quiry With referee, to.. application of the Cor- poration or the union ot Latchford tad Warrington. They were alterwards eutertained by ihga Mayor to lunch, and st.bsi fluently moseyed to Warrington Bridge. Three no a fair amount of traffic passing over the bridge at the time, but not so much as iv often the sem rho traffic Ina, Umtata, 'efficient to convince the deputation that a new bulge is imperatively required. It wee pointed out to the deputation that the two main roads on tho Booth side of the Bridge— Knutiford-road, and Wildempool Causeway- -were to he with tel by the Corporation and that a bridge, CA feet wide, without leers was rtquired in place of he pre.ont onteofteste and inadequate bridge. The deputat hoe was pleased with the improvements the Corpevetion are making. anti It is believed t these gentlemen will support the proposal el the Corporation toe • mew bridge at the next meeting of the County Council.</p>
