      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1897-12-31_WidnesExaminer_art0091" n="art0091">
        <head>DEATH OP MR. iIOLLINS ALLEN.</head>
        <p>DEATH OP MR. iIOLLINS ALLEN.</p>
        <p>'Sten, Warrlngtonian• will hear with deep re- -6elo-st.,Warvington,died Into Tuesday weeleat Can- terbury, where for about four years he has held the position of master at the School of Art. The de- ceased was a native of Warrington, and was ex- ceedingly well-known and higtly respected in thel town. He war only 29 yearn of age, and hie death hi, come as a sudden blow to his relatives and friends. Ile received his elementary education at the People's College and then attended the School of Art in the evenings for some time. In 1804 he became • day nudest, and owing to the proem. of ills studiee he was appointed • pupil teacher in 1888. Mr. Aylaud, the present headmuter,was at that time,the second master, and always fount Mr. Allen an induatrious .-turfent. and hi* disposition kindly and refined. In 188.7, Mr. Allen won the bronze medal in the National Competition for designs of tiles. It may be stated that the design with which Mr. Allen won the medal has been adopted by Messrs. Craven, Dunnill, Limited, of mobil old. Salop, and has be- come, most popular tile, it being in use in many arts of the country. In 1884, Mr. Allen was suc- cessful in obtaining the National Gold Medal for his Mmigne of carpetsmnd alse the Owen Jones memorial prise with the bronze medal of the Society of Arts. With these distinctions he was appointed to the chimes at South Newington. Continu- ing his successful career, he wee ultimately ap- pointed to the position of chief muter at Canter- bury. which lin held at the time of bin death. Mr. Allen was, perhaps, more popularly known for his connection with the cycling track. About eight years ego he wan one of the MOBt euccese- ful riders in this part rd the country, ne..l he won numerous prince. Ho married a Miss Burton of Wigan, who, together with a (welly of three children,is left to mown the premature death of her ho-bind. It, iv thought that lie. Allen caught a chills few weeks Ego whilst ettending a tuneral and pneumonia supervening he died ate stated no. Tuculay. Ihe funeral tookiplace on Friday gat Wigan.</p>
