        <p>t Warring- , Cbristmae 6ye cot bon-tires were football and Anse day,the ground Another element match between Si. which was played Widnee were the , and the team we+ aceatn- loads of apectetors. This unusual assemblage on the , eiand in the crush for admitt-' ince gates was pushed-open and gained accese to the ground In the rush which ensued re injured. Owing to the Into r • the kick-off was delayed for , would be between 10,000 and )resent when operations were use alteration took place in the ,ewas again unable to assist ' recency was filled by Hal- id, had played earlier in .he "A" team. Tn., teams I Pants, Nevitt, ninon and Douglas and Murphy, Ono., Hunter, Handley, and I male, forwards. back ; Moores, Heeeore, three-quarters; Bate and ; Deakin, Naylor, Taylor, reirhurst, and 1101, for-</p>
        <p>Owlet' deal of the referee appointed, Mr. Hancock, of IllutiVn-rn, took powsetnion of the whintic. The Monte captain lost the tow, and Taylor kicked of in • the face of a slight Miles'. Right froin the outset the game became fact and enciting. By breaking up the fret acrim nagn,Warrington Rained • foothold in Widnes territory, and Batey was called upon to wive. Illscow replied to the kick of his win 'is, but Rarratt uointan. tionally Mille ill contact with the ball, and a scrimmage wits ordered by the referee. Warrington early aeaa,geg the aggressive, but Eaten, provnd a tower of strength to . his side, his tail kicking affording much relief. A pass- ing movement by Bate, Isherwoed, and Moores gained considerable ground, but it was not until Bstey slipped when Belding thn ball, that Warrington were able to get near the Widnes line. By a vigorous rush the visiting fnrwards led by Johnson crossed the centre</p>
        <p>ooe line. A kick up the held was responded to by lamenvr,hut a mishick a moment later by Bate al- ! tams let the visitors in.+ scrimmage taking place near the Warrington line. Faul7 passing by the Widnee bneks,spoiled • certain openiths,but they retrieved their position shortly afterwards,and a pass toltispan enabled ' that player to drop • goal. Stung be this reverse, the Warringtan teem made a great effort to score, and Moores was pulled up near tae line A scrimmage near the visitors. goal posts saw the Warrington forwards I healing out,and Hallam get inn a pass made • shot at I goal hut failed. The same player, however, made amends,shortly afterwards,' or on gaining powession, he outpaced all oppultlon, unS laming to Moson that speedy torward crows i the line amid cheery. Heesom kicked a little wide in endeavouring to increase tha points. The play continued fast and exciting, and the once wan made a cracker. Toe visiting forwards ; hosing gained a foothold in the Warrington 25,a pass by Brennan to Rieman taW the latter romping over the coveted line. Bate, kinked • goal. Bali time shortly afterwards arrived, the visit ors then leading by 7 points I to thee.</p>
